{
  "key": "letter-298-part-01",
  "number": 298,
  "generationId": "01a1e905-7e56-7fe2-b2c4-ea2d1add2903",
  "voice": "Views",
  "speed": 0.9,
  "clips": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "Love.",
      "path": "audio/1971-298/01.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.726508
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "To explore truth one must be free of one's prejudices - that is, from oneself.",
      "path": "audio/1971-298/02.mp3",
      "start": 2.01059,
      "end": 7.027823
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "Otherwise one goes round and round in circles, because the known can never be the door for the unknown; and the known is the mind so mind becomes the barrier.",
      "path": "audio/1971-298/03.mp3",
      "start": 8.290522000000001,
      "end": 17.628503000000002
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "Look attentively at this fact.",
      "path": "audio/1971-298/04.mp3",
      "start": 18.929206,
      "end": 20.913673
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "Be alert to the vicious circle of the mind - and then there is transcendence.",
      "path": "audio/1971-298/05.mp3",
      "start": 22.550248999999997,
      "end": 27.485238000000003
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "The known must cease for the unknown to be.",
      "path": "audio/1971-298/06.mp3",
      "start": 29.031882,
      "end": 31.862585
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "The known must go for the unknown to come in - and this cessation of the known is meditation.",
      "path": "audio/1971-298/07.mp3",
      "start": 33.376553,
      "end": 40.07
    }
  ]
}
